        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a185" ANNOTATION_REF="a3">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's what you can speak about.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a186" ANNOTATION_REF="a4">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>When a new baby boy is born, it is never</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a187" ANNOTATION_REF="a5">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Her uncles seemed to be evil people.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a188" ANNOTATION_REF="a6">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>There was just one person that was doing that, but maybe there were more.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a189" ANNOTATION_REF="a7">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As soon as the baby was born, the uncle would go to see if it was a girl.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a190" ANNOTATION_REF="a8">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If it was a girl, they would just leave the baby alone.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a191" ANNOTATION_REF="a9">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If it was a boy, they would kill it.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a192" ANNOTATION_REF="a10">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>None of the boys were left alive to grow.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a193" ANNOTATION_REF="a11">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then, one day, another girl had a baby, and she hid the baby boy's thing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a194" ANNOTATION_REF="a12">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when the uncle got there, he felt the baby to make sure it was really a girl, and then he left it alone and went away.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a195" ANNOTATION_REF="a13">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they heard the baby when it cried.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a196" ANNOTATION_REF="a14">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“That baby that's crying really sounds like a boy.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a197" ANNOTATION_REF="a15">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You'd better go examine it again.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a198" ANNOTATION_REF="a16">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So again, they went to do that, and they arrived there.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a199" ANNOTATION_REF="a17">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, they asked again if it was really a girl.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a200" ANNOTATION_REF="a18">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“It's really a girl, a girl”, the mother said.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a201" ANNOTATION_REF="a19">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Eventually, she decided to flee.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a202" ANNOTATION_REF="a20">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Very early in the morning, she left, walking.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a203" ANNOTATION_REF="a21">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Was it the chief that was doing all that?
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a204" ANNOTATION_REF="a22">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Aha, he was a warrior.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a205" ANNOTATION_REF="a23">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He did those bad things for whatever reason.Maybe he was uneasy about [losing his status,] whatever.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a206" ANNOTATION_REF="a24">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he killed them, like how the First People used to kill each other.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a207" ANNOTATION_REF="a25">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so that woman fled, walking upstream.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a208" ANNOTATION_REF="a26">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>She kept walking until she arrived to shxuxeey'elu.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a209" ANNOTATION_REF="a27">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the baby was crying, and that's where she bathed him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a210" ANNOTATION_REF="a28">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After she finished bathing the child, then she started walking again until she reached Quamichan.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a211" ANNOTATION_REF="a29">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she bathed him again, and she had a shell, whatever kind of shell—horse clam or whatever.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a212" ANNOTATION_REF="a30">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They were different then,  
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a213" ANNOTATION_REF="a31">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>She laid him down and prepared [a bath], put water in a container, and she bathed her baby.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a214" ANNOTATION_REF="a32">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why it's referred to as Little Dish, that place on your land.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a215" ANNOTATION_REF="a33">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's a little dish.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a216" ANNOTATION_REF="a34">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After all that she did, she started to walk again, and she came uphill towards Amelia Bob's place, getting to where the church was.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a217" ANNOTATION_REF="a35">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What's the name of that place? St. Peter's Church.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a218" ANNOTATION_REF="a36">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Reaching that place, her baby was crying non-stop again.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a219" ANNOTATION_REF="a37">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And she bathed him again, using that shell.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a220" ANNOTATION_REF="a38">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And again, she filled it with water, and again she bathed her child.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a221" ANNOTATION_REF="a39">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After she finished doing that, she started walking again.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a222" ANNOTATION_REF="a40">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And thus, they named that place ts'e'wi'tun.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a223" ANNOTATION_REF="a41">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why they are calling that place ts'e'wi'tun.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a224" ANNOTATION_REF="a42">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>St. Peters, 	ts'e'wi'tun.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a225" ANNOTATION_REF="a43">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yes, and the one at your land is the little dish, the small one, and its name means small.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a226" ANNOTATION_REF="a44">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then again, she started to walk.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a227" ANNOTATION_REF="a45">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she started to follow the creek, here to hwkw'sutsum.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a228" ANNOTATION_REF="a46">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she got as far as a place over there.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a229" ANNOTATION_REF="a47">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And indeed, there was a big rock in that place where she was, and they camped out there, building their home.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a230" ANNOTATION_REF="a48">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Where they lived was a good place for catching trout for them to eat.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a231" ANNOTATION_REF="a49">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then... no, I jumped in my story and got ahead in what I said.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a232" ANNOTATION_REF="a50">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I got too far ahead.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a233" ANNOTATION_REF="a51">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He kept bathing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a234" ANNOTATION_REF="a52">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He was bathing... I'll keep going.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a235" ANNOTATION_REF="a53">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He kept bathing.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a236" ANNOTATION_REF="a54">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He scrubbed himself, scrubbed with the boughs.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a237" ANNOTATION_REF="a55">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when he was doing that, he would shake the boughs.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a238" ANNOTATION_REF="a56">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when they hit in the water, they started to swim.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a239" ANNOTATION_REF="a57">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The nettles from the boughs started to swim.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a240" ANNOTATION_REF="a58">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They hit the water, and what was swimming turned into trout.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a241" ANNOTATION_REF="a59">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Every time he bathed, that happened.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a242" ANNOTATION_REF="a60">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He shook the branch, and the nettles hit the water and would start swimming.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a243" ANNOTATION_REF="a61">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They would turn into trout, little trout, fingerlings.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a244" ANNOTATION_REF="a62">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, this is where the trout came from.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a245" ANNOTATION_REF="a63">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It's because of Q'ise'q taking a bath that the trout appeared.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a246" ANNOTATION_REF="a64">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He's telling this story clearly; good.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a247" ANNOTATION_REF="a65">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why the trout is here at Quamichan.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a248" ANNOTATION_REF="a66">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And perhaps that's why that place is known as Hwkw'sutsum, 'place full of trout'.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a249" ANNOTATION_REF="a67">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That big boulder is there, and that's Q'ise'q's mother.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a250" ANNOTATION_REF="a68">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And that's where he was growing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a251" ANNOTATION_REF="a69">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then the mother warned him, “Don't go too far that way, son.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a252" ANNOTATION_REF="a70">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Just stay close by when you play.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a253" ANNOTATION_REF="a71">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He was holding a bow and arrow that was prepared for him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a254" ANNOTATION_REF="a72">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he started hunting the birds, fixing them, pulling the skins off the birds, and they were sewn together to make an outfit.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a255" ANNOTATION_REF="a73">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>All the different species of birds that he killed were in his outfit.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a256" ANNOTATION_REF="a74">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he arrived at that place where he was bathed.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a257" ANNOTATION_REF="a75">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was getting strong and becoming a young man.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a258" ANNOTATION_REF="a76">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He lay down on the bluffs, where it was beautiful, just lying there, reclining.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a259" ANNOTATION_REF="a77">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>At hwkw'ukw'uqe'num'.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a260" ANNOTATION_REF="a78">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And something came flying by, and it saw the beautiful outfit that he had on, warming himself on the bluff.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a261" ANNOTATION_REF="a79">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he came flying down, circling around him.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a262" ANNOTATION_REF="a80">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He circled around him again, and then he came down and landed near him.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a263" ANNOTATION_REF="a81">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he went close to the one that was lying on his back, and spoke to him, “Your outfit is very beautiful.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a264" ANNOTATION_REF="a82">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I'm really wanting your outfit.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a265" ANNOTATION_REF="a83">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I want to take your outfit, and you can exchange it for my outfit.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a266" ANNOTATION_REF="a84">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And if you agree and put it on, you will be able to fly, the way I was flying before I landed.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a267" ANNOTATION_REF="a85">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he says “I really want my outfit.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a268" ANNOTATION_REF="a86">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“But I'm really wanting your outfit.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a269" ANNOTATION_REF="a87">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Well, perhaps if you really want it, I will give it to you and...”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a270" ANNOTATION_REF="a88">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Ah, okay! And if you use this, you can try to fly; go and do it now.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a271" ANNOTATION_REF="a89">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he put it on; Q'ise'q did put it on.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a272" ANNOTATION_REF="a90">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so, he told him, “Try to do it like this, then.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a273" ANNOTATION_REF="a91">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he did this, and he started to tremble.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a274" ANNOTATION_REF="a92">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he started to fly, Q'ise'q did.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a275" ANNOTATION_REF="a93">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was told that he had done enough and to go back and return.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a276" ANNOTATION_REF="a94">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh, you're good! You did good.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a277" ANNOTATION_REF="a95">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“You did it just the way I told you.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a278" ANNOTATION_REF="a96">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Okay, you can have my outfit then.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a279" ANNOTATION_REF="a97">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Good.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a280" ANNOTATION_REF="a98">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, they traded, and the one that was flying wore Q'ise'q's outfit, and he ended up just walking.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a281" ANNOTATION_REF="a99">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And Q'ise'q was able to fly.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a282" ANNOTATION_REF="a100">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And Q'ise'q just flew off, and he went to where his mother was.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a283" ANNOTATION_REF="a101">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he went flying, circling around his mother.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a284" ANNOTATION_REF="a102">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What he was wearing made a loud flapping sound.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a285" ANNOTATION_REF="a103">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The noise of his outfit was quite loud.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a286" ANNOTATION_REF="a104">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he would just hide his outfit.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a287" ANNOTATION_REF="a105">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he would just walk home to his mother.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a288" ANNOTATION_REF="a106">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He arrived and she told him, “Son, whatever was that, I wonder, that was that was flying around?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a289" ANNOTATION_REF="a107">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It came around here, and I got really scared.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a290" ANNOTATION_REF="a108">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he pretended that he didn't know what it was, even though it was actually him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a291" ANNOTATION_REF="a109">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then he started thinking that he wanted to go to the place that his mother forbade him ever to go to.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a292" ANNOTATION_REF="a110">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Okay, I'm going to go take a look.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a293" ANNOTATION_REF="a111">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so, on the next day, he went off.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a294" ANNOTATION_REF="a112">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he arrived there.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a295" ANNOTATION_REF="a113">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he didn't really show himself; he just landed.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a296" ANNOTATION_REF="a114">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he saw the ones playing a ball game called qi'qtum'as, either qi'qtum'as or, what is is called, ts'uqwula'.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a297" ANNOTATION_REF="a115">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think what they were playing was called ts'uqwula'.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a298" ANNOTATION_REF="a116">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>A deer's tail was attached to it, and they were throwing it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a299" ANNOTATION_REF="a117">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they were catching it just like a baseball.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a300" ANNOTATION_REF="a118">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The tail was attached to it, and it would be thrown to their own team.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a301" ANNOTATION_REF="a119">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the one that catches it would run.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a302" ANNOTATION_REF="a120">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The knot of a tree was what they made their ball from.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a303" ANNOTATION_REF="a121">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It was from the vine maple tree.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a304" ANNOTATION_REF="a122">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think it was the vine maple tree that you find that kind of [knot].</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a305" ANNOTATION_REF="a123">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the deer tail was attached to it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a306" ANNOTATION_REF="a124">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the deer tail was attached to it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a307" ANNOTATION_REF="a125">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And that's how... what is it called... the thing they were throwing was identified.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a308" ANNOTATION_REF="a126">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when they catch it, they run with it.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a309" ANNOTATION_REF="a127">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It's really like a scrimmage.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a310" ANNOTATION_REF="a128">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It's like a scrimmage when they scramble for it.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a311" ANNOTATION_REF="a129">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they were running from one end to the other.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a312" ANNOTATION_REF="a130">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and he was watching.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a313" ANNOTATION_REF="a131">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he found out about them, and then he went back home.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a314" ANNOTATION_REF="a132">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he started to look for a weapon, thinking he was going to kill his uncles.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a315" ANNOTATION_REF="a133">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That is where he was from before he came to the place they fled to, where his mother fled with him.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a316" ANNOTATION_REF="a134">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It had been really forbidden, and he already knew what had happened.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a317" ANNOTATION_REF="a135">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he cut down some wood that was pole-like to make a club with.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a318" ANNOTATION_REF="a136">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was testing it on the rock.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a319" ANNOTATION_REF="a137">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>But the stick would just break.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a320" ANNOTATION_REF="a138">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He clubbed the rock, and it would just smash, break.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a321" ANNOTATION_REF="a139">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He did this until he found one that was good.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a322" ANNOTATION_REF="a140">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think that was yew that he found.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a323" ANNOTATION_REF="a141">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he cut it and tried it, and the rock broke.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a324" ANNOTATION_REF="a142">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What he prepared was quite long, and one end was thicker.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a325" ANNOTATION_REF="a143">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he made it into his club.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a326" ANNOTATION_REF="a144">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the next thing he did was to go to where his alleged uncles were.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a327" ANNOTATION_REF="a145">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they were all playing again.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a328" ANNOTATION_REF="a146">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he arrived there, flying.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a329" ANNOTATION_REF="a147">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he knew where they were coming from.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a330" ANNOTATION_REF="a148">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And it was like that; he went toward where they were going.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a331" ANNOTATION_REF="a149">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he clubbed the ones that were running, breaking their heads.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a332" ANNOTATION_REF="a150">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And was clubbing them as they were running</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a333" ANNOTATION_REF="a151">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>While he was flying, they were just running.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a334" ANNOTATION_REF="a152">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was hitting them on their heads.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a335" ANNOTATION_REF="a153">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>When the club hit their heads, they would split open.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a336" ANNOTATION_REF="a154">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Their heads were rocks, and that's what he was doing to the Stoneheads.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a337" ANNOTATION_REF="a155">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Raphael Johnny is always saying that Stoneheads are crazy.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a338" ANNOTATION_REF="a156">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And maybe it's true.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a339" ANNOTATION_REF="a157">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Is it over here at Greenpoint?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a340" ANNOTATION_REF="a158">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's right, over at Xinupsum, Kw'etqum'</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a341" ANNOTATION_REF="a159">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's the one called Kw'etqum', where the water was over there; that was their water.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a342" ANNOTATION_REF="a160">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That running water came from up above, and it hit the.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a343" ANNOTATION_REF="a161">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I guess this water is dry now.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a344" ANNOTATION_REF="a162">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It's maybe..</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a345" ANNOTATION_REF="a163">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Over at Kw'etqum'.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a346" ANNOTATION_REF="a164">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah, that water is Kw'etqum'.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a347" ANNOTATION_REF="a165">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, maybe that was Samuel's place.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a348" ANNOTATION_REF="a166">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's where the home of the Stoneheads was.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a349" ANNOTATION_REF="a167">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And his uncles all perished.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a350" ANNOTATION_REF="a168">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He clubbed them, and their heads burst.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a351" ANNOTATION_REF="a169">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they just perished; he finished off his uncles, and he landed where his house used to be.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a352" ANNOTATION_REF="a170">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was told that he would be given a young lady.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a353" ANNOTATION_REF="a171">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so, the girls were lined up.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a354" ANNOTATION_REF="a172">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he didn't want the eldest.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a355" ANNOTATION_REF="a173">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It was only the youngest one, who was called Scabby Head.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a356" ANNOTATION_REF="a174">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's the one he chose.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a357" ANNOTATION_REF="a175">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's the one he wanted.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a358" ANNOTATION_REF="a176">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>All the young ladies primped.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a359" ANNOTATION_REF="a177">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, the girls made themselves pretty, applying ochre on their cheeks.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a360" ANNOTATION_REF="a178">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>But it wasn't one of the pretty ones.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a361" ANNOTATION_REF="a179">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It was just Scabby Head, right at the end.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a362" ANNOTATION_REF="a180">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's the one he wanted and took.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a363" ANNOTATION_REF="a181">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so that's end of that, and that story is finished.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a364" ANNOTATION_REF="a182">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE/>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
    </TIER>
